# Response headers for the static assets, read natively by Workers assets.
#
# Every rule here is keyed on an asset path. The crawler directives for `/view`
# and `/d/*` are not — those paths have no file — so they live in
# `robotsTagForRoute` in `src/router.ts` and are set by the Worker. `robots.txt`
# asks crawlers to stay out of both; a Disallow is a request, an `X-Robots-Tag`
# is an instruction to the indexer.
#
# ## The Content-Security-Policy
#
# This app renders JSON that people paste from production systems, so a policy
# is worth having even though every render path builds DOM or escapes on the way
# into markup. It is defence in depth: the thing that stops the *next* injection
# bug from becoming an exfiltration.
#
# It can be this tight because the app loads nothing from anywhere else. Every
# font is self-hosted under `/assets`, there is no analytics, no CDN and no
# third-party anything.
#
#   default-src 'none'    deny by default; every allowed kind is listed below
#   script-src 'self'     one module from /assets. The JSON-LD block in
#                         index.html is a data block, not executable script,
#                         so it is not subject to this
#   style-src 'self'      one stylesheet. No 'unsafe-inline': the single inline
#                         style attribute this document used to carry (the
#                         noscript fallback) now lives in styles.css, precisely
#                         so this can stay closed. `clipboard.ts` sets `.style`
#                         through the CSSOM, which CSP does not govern
#   font-src 'self'       the self-hosted woff2 faces
#   img-src 'self'        the icons and the OG image. No `data:`: nothing uses
#                         one, and `assetsInlineLimit: 0` in vite.config.ts
#                         means the build never inlines an asset as one either
#   connect-src 'self'    /api/shares, the only request the client ever makes
#   manifest-src 'self'   site.webmanifest, linked from index.html
#   base-uri 'none'       nothing may retarget relative URLs
#   form-action 'none'    there is no form that submits anywhere
#   frame-ancestors 'none'  nobody frames a tool that renders your payloads
#
# `X-Frame-Options: DENY` alongside `frame-ancestors` for anything too old to
# honour the latter. Where they disagree, `frame-ancestors` wins.

/*
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self'; font-src 'self'; img-src 'self'; connect-src 'self'; manifest-src 'self'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'
  X-Frame-Options: DENY

# `/d/*` and `/view` used to be given `X-Robots-Tag` here. They are not files:
# neither has an asset of its own, so the Worker builds their response from
# `index.html` and a rule keyed on those paths never matched. The table moved to
# `robotsTagForRoute` in `src/router.ts`, which the Worker reads — `test/seo.test.ts`
# checks the two paths still get their directives.

# Every file here is content-hashed by the build (`assetsInlineLimit: 0`, and
# Vite's own naming), so a given URL's bytes never change — a new build means a
# new URL. `immutable` is what that earns: the browser stops revalidating on
# every load, which it was doing under the site-wide `max-age=0`.

# A stylesheet's own subresources (the four .woff2 faces) take their Referrer-Policy from the
# STYLESHEET'S response, not from the page that linked it. A share page is `no-referrer` (QA4),
# but the CSS it loads was served with the site-wide `strict-origin-when-cross-origin`, so each
# font request went out with `Referer: <https://…/assets/index-….css>` (QA7 P1). That URL carries
# no share id or key, so nothing leaked, but REGRESSION §8 says "no Referer" and a rule that is
# true except for fonts is the kind nobody re-checks. Detach, then set, so exactly one value
# leaves (a joined `a, b` value would still resolve to the last token, but one is cleaner).
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
  ! Referrer-Policy
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer

/sitemap.xml
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600
/robots.txt
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600
/llms.txt
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600
/llms-full.txt
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600
